  "worked_solution": "We find the constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(1)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n2={c}_{1}.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{\u2032}(1)=-4,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{\u2032}(x) & =({c}_{1}+3{c}_{2})\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(3\\operatorname{ln}\u2061t)+({c}_{2}-3{c}_{1})\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3\\operatorname{ln}\u2061t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{\u2032}(1)=-4$ and ${c}_{1}=2$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4 & =2+3{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(t)=2t(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(3\\operatorname{ln}\u2061t)-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3\\operatorname{ln}\u2061t)).\n$$",
